# Git stores what is on disk, byte for byte, and hands it back unchanged.
#
# The previous setting was `* text=auto eol=lf`, which rewrote line endings on
# the way in and announced it on every commit from a Windows machine. A file
# should be what it is; normalising it is an edit nobody asked for.
* -text

# The one exception, and it is not cosmetic: CI runs these on Linux, where a
# carriage return at the end of a shebang or a command makes bash fail with
# something that reads as a missing command rather than a line-ending problem.
*.sh text eol=lf

*.png binary
*.torrent binary
